<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jim Bolger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1935">1935</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as James Brendan Bolger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jim Bolger was Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> from 1990 to 1997, leading the Fourth National Government. His government continued the free-market reforms begun by Labour, with welfare cuts and labour-market deregulation under finance minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruth-richardson">Ruth Richardson</a>. He also began the major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-waitangi">Treaty of Waitangi</a> settlements with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikato-tainui">Waikato-Tainui</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngai-tahu">Ngāi Tahu</a>, and after the adoption of MMP formed a coalition with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand-first">New Zealand First</a> in 1996.</p></div>
